t-analysis", "publisher": "CertiK", "artifact": {"path": "reports/cohort_rebuild_v2/http/00d025dd202388338feee5f0b9f13f352439d645540ca046d0d0eb7ddb4f0919.gz", "sha256": "19c6faf653539095be7d45ec732a1d8fc6347b64059e2fae7dcbb661423ed732"}, "text": "Nomad Bridge, a cross-chain bridge between Ethereum, Moonbeam, Avalanche, Evmos and Milkomeda was exploited for ~$190M. Nomad Bridge, a cross-chain bridge between Ethereum, Moonbeam, Avalanche, Evmos and Milkomeda was exploited for ~$190M. idge experienced an exploit causing a loss of around $190M worth of assets. The vulnerability was in the initialization process where the “committedRoot” is set as ZERO. Therefore, the attackers were able to bypass the message verification process and drain the tokens from the bridge contract. Summary Nomad Bridge, a cross-chain bridge between Ethereum, Moonbeam, Avalanche, Evmos and Milkomeda was exploited for ~$190M. The exploit occured when a routine upgrade allowed verification messages to be bypassed on Nomad. Attackers abused this to copy/paste transactions and were able to drain the bridge of nearly all funds before it could be stopped. Protocol Details: Nomad Brid systematically drain the bridge’s funds over a long series of transactions.The vulnerability was in the initialization process where the “committedRoot” is set as ZERO. Therefore, the attacker was able to bypass the message verification process and drain the tokens from the bridge contract. Due to this flawed upgrade, users could exploit bridge funds by copying the original hacker's transaction calldata and replacing the original address with a personal one. The transaction then processed and successfully removed funds from the bridge. At this time, ~$190M has been exploited. In four hours, other hackers, bots, and community members replicated the initial attack, drainin"}]}, {"id": "445335fb34e4b055", "poc_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SunWeb3Sec/DeFiHackLabs/main/src/test/2022-10/ATK_exp.sol", "poc_artifact"